{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Pharaoh's chariots and his host.</b> 'Pharaoh's chariots' are the six hundred choice chariots he took from Egypt; 'and his host' — this is the chariots of Egypt; 'the choice of his officers' — this is 'and his officers over all of them.' And since Scripture should properly have said, 'Pharaoh's chariots and his host He cast into the Sea of Reeds, and the choice of his officers sank in it,' it may be explained that Pharaoh's chariots were judged in the upper sea, and therefore sank in the Sea of Reefs below. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: with the measure a man measures, it is measured to him. He decreed (Exodus 1:22): 'Every son that is born, cast him into the river' — therefore, 'Pharaoh's chariots and his host He cast into the sea.' He decreed (ibid.): 'and you shall see them upon the stones' — therefore they went down into the depths like a stone."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:17.929701322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}